{"name":"There’s No Place Like Home","hex":"#ad9569","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"there","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["In or at a place or location (stated, implied or otherwise indicated) that is perceived to be away from, or at a relative distance from, the speaker (compare here).","At that point, stage, etc., visualised as a distinct place."]},{"part":"Interjection","definitions":["Used to offer encouragement or sympathy; see also there, there and there now.","Used to express victory or completion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/there"},{"term":"place","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An area; somewhere within an area.\nAn open space, particularly a city square, market square, or courtyard.\n\n A street, sometimes but not always surrounding a public place, square, or plaza of the same name.","An open space, particularly a city square, market square, or courtyard."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To put (someone or something) in a specific location.","To earn a given spot in a competition; to rank at a certain position ()."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/place"},{"term":"like","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To enjoy, be pleased by; favor; be in favor of.","To please ."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Something that a person likes (prefers).","An individual vote showing support for, approval of, or enjoyment of, something posted on the Internet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/like"}],"entries":[{"title":"Like Home","blocks":[{"text":"\"Like Home\" is a song by Dutch DJ and producer Nicky Romero and Australian twin sisters Nervo. It was the third single released from Romero's label, Protocol Recordings. It was also the second song from the label to top the Beatport Top 100 chart. It peaked at number 33 on the UK Singles Chart."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/0/05/Like_Home_by_Nicky_Romero_and_NERVO.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Like_Home","wikidata":"Q6356543"},{"title":"No Place","blocks":[{"text":"No Place is a small village that lies between the towns of Stanley and Beamish, in County Durham, England. It lies near to the Beamish Mary coal pit, just to the south of the A693 road. The local church is known as the \"Tin Chapel\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Beamish_Mary_Inn_built_1897_in_No_Place.jpg/330px-Beamish_Mary_Inn_built_1897_in_No_Place.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/No_Place","wikidata":"Q7044768"},{"title":"Like","blocks":[{"text":"In English, the word like has a very wide range of uses, both conventional and non-standard. It can be used as a noun, verb, adverb, adjective, preposition, particle, conjunction, hedge, filler, quotative, and semi-suffix."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Like","wikidata":"Q3249878"},{"title":"Home","blocks":[{"text":"A home, or domicile, is a space used as a permanent or semi-permanent residence for one or more human occupants, and sometimes various companion animals. Homes provide sheltered spaces, for instance rooms, where domestic activity can be performed such as sleeping, preparing food, eating, and hygiene as well as providing spaces for work and leisure such as remote working, studying, and playing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/SearsHouse115.jpg/330px-SearsHouse115.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Home","wikidata":"Q7743"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/No_Place_..._Like_a_Co-operative_Home%5E_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1012470.jpg/500px-No_Place_..._Like_a_Co-operative_Home%5E_-_geograph.org.uk_-_1012470.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&ut